Refresh lock: show a swapped buffer at the next round, and time the rounds by the clock

Two things kept a compositor that waits in its swap (WESTEROS_GL_USE_REFRESH_LOCK)
on a device without vertical blank events (WESTEROS_GL_NO_VBLANK) at about
half the display's refresh rate:

- The swap marked its window dirty only after the refresh thread had let it
  go, so the buffer was shown one round later than it could be, and each
  picture took two rounds. It is marked before the wait now: the next round
  shows the buffer and then lets the swap go.
- Without a vertical blank to wait for, the refresh thread slept a fixed time
  after each round's work: three quarters of a refresh interval when it had
  shown something, a whole one when not. A round was therefore not a refresh
  interval long. The sleep now ends at the next multiple of the interval.

Measured in the tv-emu virtual machine (virtio-gpu, Mesa's llvmpipe, 1920x1080
at 60): RDK's window manager showed 35 pictures a second before.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c b/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c
index c64cf9d..ee7f146 100644
--- a/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c
+++ b/westeros-gl/westeros-gl.c
@@ -5976,6 +5976,7 @@ static void *wstRefreshThread( void *arg )
    WstGLCtx *ctx= (WstGLCtx*)arg;
    drmVBlank vbl;
    long long delay;
+   long long nextRound= 0LL;
    long long refreshInterval= 0LL;
    long long vblankTime= 0LL;
    #ifdef USE_EXTERNAL_STATS
@@ -6083,7 +6084,28 @@ static void *wstRefreshThread( void *arg )
       {
          if ( delay )
          {
-            usleep( delay );
+            /* Without a vertical blank to wait for, the rounds are timed by
+               the clock, one each refresh interval. Sleeping a fixed time
+               after each round's work, as it was, gave rounds of the work
+               plus three quarters of an interval when something was shown
+               and of a whole interval when not. */
+            long long now= getMonotonicTimeMicros();
+            if ( refreshInterval > 0 )
+            {
+               nextRound += refreshInterval;
+               if ( nextRound > now )
+               {
+                  usleep( nextRound-now );
+               }
+               else
+               {
+                  nextRound= now;
+               }
+            }
+            else
+            {
+               usleep( delay );
+            }
          }
       }
    }
@@ -7703,15 +7725,19 @@ EGLAPI EGLBoolean eglSwapBuffers( EGLDisplay dpy, EGLSurface surface )
             if ( gRealGLFinish ) gRealGLFinish();
             result= gRealEGLSwapBuffers( dpy, surface );
             pthread_mutex_lock( &nwIter->mutexRefresh );
+            /* The window is dirty from here on, so that the refresh thread's
+               next round shows this buffer and then lets the swap go. Marked
+               only after the wait, as it was, a buffer was shown a round
+               later than it could be: two rounds for each picture. */
+            TRACE3("mark nw %p dirty", nwIter);
+            gCtx->dirty= true;
+            nwIter->dirty= true;
             pthread_cond_wait( &nwIter->condRefresh, &nwIter->mutexRefresh );
         } else {
              result= gRealEGLSwapBuffers( dpy, surface );
          }
          if ( nwIter )
          {
-            TRACE3("mark nw %p dirty", nwIter);
-            gCtx->dirty= true;
-            nwIter->dirty= true;
             pthread_mutex_unlock( &nwIter->mutexRefresh );
          }
       }
